# Conclusion

## Verdict

```julia; echo = false, results = "tex"
print(acceptance_conclusion_text())
```

## Summary by scenario

Every scenario of this report, the number of comparisons it made against reference values
and the number of recorded outcomes that failed.

  * `API-JOURNAL` makes no comparison of its own: its outcomes state that the journal is
    present and that every one of its records passed. The records themselves are in
    `test/references/testlog.csv`.
  * `PKG-TEST` makes no numeric comparison either: its single outcome is the result of the
    package test suite, so a failure there means the suite failed.
  * `VAL-MM`, `VAL-BE` and `VAL-SPSS` report the count of checks their procedures ran,
    followed by one outcome per failure.
  * A required scenario whose code chunk errored out produces no rows at all and is listed
    as NOT REPORTED; its results table is then missing from the chapter above as well.

```julia; echo = false, results = "tex"
print(acceptance_md(acceptance_summary_table()))
```
Table: Comparisons and verdict by scenario

## Divergence journal

Everything that failed acceptance, from both sources: the rows of the API check journal that
did not pass, and the records the report made itself. A comparison row carries the computed
value, the reference value, their difference and the limit it was judged against.

```julia; echo = false, results = "tex"
print(acceptance_journal_block())
```

```julia; echo = false, results = "tex"
# The Conclusion marks itself once its tables are rendered. A chunk that errored out records
# nothing, so a report that lost its verdict is caught by the required-scenario check outside
# the document generator. The mark is made before the log is written, so that the files
# written here already carry it.
acceptance_mark("CONCLUSION", true, "conclusion rendered")
acc, div = acceptance_write_journal()
print("Full acceptance log: `docs/src/validation_acceptance.tsv`. " *
      "Divergence journal: `docs/src/validation_divergences.tsv`. " *
      "Per-check journal of the API suite: `test/references/testlog.csv`.")
```

